    {
      "id": "c1",
      "kind": "concept",
      "figure": "coordinate-plane",
      "body": "Two points also fix a line. Work in order: first the **slope**, m = (y₂ − y₁)/(x₂ − x₁). Then use **either point** to get b = y₁ − m·x₁. Then write **y = mx + b**, and confirm both points fit."
    },
    {
      "id": "i1",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Two points pin a line down completely.",
      "widget": {
        "type": "lineExplore",
        "targetSlope": 2,
        "targetIntercept": -1,
        "slopeMin": -4,
        "slopeMax": 4,
        "interceptMin": -5,
        "interceptMax": 5,
        "slopeStart": 0,
        "interceptStart": 0,
        "gridMax": 6,
        "prompt": "Build the line through (1, 1) and (3, 5).",
        "successFeedback": "y = 2x − 1. From (1, 1) to (3, 5) the rise is 4 and the run is 2, so the slope is 2 — and only one intercept then drops the line onto both points. Two points, two unknowns, one line.",
        "slopeFeedback": "The steepness is off: from (1, 1) to (3, 5) is 4 up for 2 across.",
        "interceptFeedback": "The slope is right, but the line misses the points. Slide it until it passes through both."
      },
      "predict": {
        "prompt": "Your line must pass through two given points. How many different lines can do that?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "one",
            "label": "Exactly one"
          },
          {
            "id": "two",
            "label": "Two"
          },
          {
            "id": "many",
            "label": "Infinitely many"
          }
        ],
        "outcomeId": "one",
        "reveal": "Two points pin a line completely: the slope is forced (rise over run between them), and once the slope is set, the intercept is forced too. That's why two points are always enough to write y = mx + b — unless they share an x-value, like (1, 2) and (1, 5): still exactly one line through them, but it's the vertical line x = 1, whose slope is undefined and which no y = mx + b can write."
      },
      "conceptTag": "line-from-two-points",
